611	  /**
612	   * Update an existing issue.
613	   *
614	   * Appends an update event to the issue file, recomputes state, and updates the index.
615	   * Handles hierarchy side effects: downward cascade (auto-close done children when parent
616	   * closes), upward promotion (promote parent when child advances past it), and reparenting
617	   * validation. Also auto-resolves active blockages when the issue transitions to done/closed.
618	   *
619	   * @param id - The issue ID to update
620	   * @param params - Update parameters (at least one field required besides author)
621	   * @param params.title - New title
622	   * @param params.description - New description
623	   * @param params.status - New status
624	   * @param params.assignee - New assignee, or null to clear
625	   * @param params.tags - New tags (replaces existing)
626	   * @param params.priority - New priority (1-5)
627	   * @param params.parentId - New parent ID, or null to detach
628	   * @param params.author - Override author (resolved by auth layer if not provided)
629	   * @returns `{ result: "OK" }` on success, or a AgentrackError on auth failure
630	   * @throws {AgentrackError} NOT_INITIALIZED if no `.agentrack/` directory
631	   * @throws {AgentrackError} INVALID_PARAMS if no fields provided besides author
632	   * @throws {AgentrackError} NOT_FOUND if issue ID is not in the index
633	   * @throws {AgentrackError} ISSUE_MISSING if index entry exists but file is missing
634	   * @throws {AgentrackError} HIERARCHY_CONSTRAINT if status change violates parent/child rules
635	   *
